<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bugey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bugey is a historical region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ain">Ain department</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, between the Jura mountains and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a>, with Belley as its chief town. Long held by the counts and dukes of Savoy, it was ceded to France with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bresse">Bresse</a> and Gex by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> in 1601 in exchange for the Marquisate of Saluzzo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bugey.jpg" alt="Bugey" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rolf Süssbrich · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Colombier,_Ain,_France.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
